nths (larger R&D budgets). Counter-move: \u22121.5.\n- Reflexivity: positive \u2014 buybacks ($2B auth) + strong FCF support the\n  equity currency for M&A; SBC-heavy comp is the negative feedback (dilution\n  ~8% of rev/yr, offset by buybacks).\n- Customer evolution: mid-market is mainstream, not early-adopter; LTV/CAC\n  healthy (broker channel >25% of new business); AI usage doubling QoQ\n  [Actual] is early-stage monetization, not yet revenue [Assumption].\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior: Layer 1.5 base rates. Updates: FY27 guide (lower growth, flat\nmargins), $2B buyback, Aidora/Grayscale (margin drag), macro hike-risk.\nPosterior scenarios:\n- BEAR 25%: FY27 6.1% \u2192 2% by FY31; GAAP OI mgn 21.5\u219221.0%; WACC 9.5%;\n  OE CAGR ~3%. IV \u2248 $92 (with buyback ~$97). Trigger: employment recession\n  + Rippling price war + retention <90%.\n- BASE 50%: as Layer 3. IV \u2248 $125.\n- BULL 25%: FY27 7.3% (beat) \u2192 6% by FY31; OI mgn \u2192 25.5%; WACC 8.5%;\n  OE CAGR ~10.6%. IV \u2248 $156 (with buyback ~$165). Trigger: AI ARPU\n  acceleration, retention >93%, 3+ points share gain, two Fed cuts.\n- Probabilities sum 100%; base is modal.\nEXPECTED VALUE: 0.25\u00d797 + 0.50\u00d7125 + 0.25\u00d7165 \u2248 $128 (buyback-adjusted);\n0.25\u00d792 + 0.50\u00d7118 + 0.25\u00d7147 \u2248 $118.8 (current-share basis). Use\n$124.5 midpoint.\nMoS = ($125 \u2212 $152.77)/$125 = \u221222% \u2192 NONE. 50% CI \u2248 $108\u2013141; 80% CI\n\u2248 $92\u2013165. Downside asymmetry: \u221240% worst vs +8% base.\n