ome valid if AI attach visibly lifts ARPU\nto 7%+ while retention >93%. \"Float income is a moat\" \u2014 valid only while\nrates stay high; it is not recurring-software economics.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (37-point, summarized)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nA. Methodology: PASS \u2014 engine justified (Layer 0); no DCF-only or\n   multiple-only conclusion; cash-flow definition explicit (OE basis).\nB. Valuation: PASS with flags \u2014 WACC 9.0% [Assumption] is the largest\n   uncertainty; beta 0.433 vendor figure REJECTED with stated reason.\nC. Bias: PASS \u2014 no base-rate overshoot; short thesis written from same data;\n   sell-side targets not adopted as fair value.\nD. Consistency: PASS \u2014 T0 vs T-1 vs Tpf time-points separated; no mixing of\n   GAAP/reported-FCF/owner-earnings without labels.\nE. Narrative: PASS \u2014 \"AI platform\" narrative not valued beyond assumption-\n   tagged ARPU path; float income excluded from core economics.\nF. Red team: PASS \u2014 7-bullet short thesis + logic combat + adversarial data.\nG. Data integrity: TWO UNRESOLVED ITEMS \u2014 (1) capex definition gap: filed\n   PP&E-only $36M vs vendor $105M; I used broad $105M and disclosed; (2)\n   vendor total debt $133M vs filed LT debt $81M; reconciled via $52M\n   operating leases and disclosed. Analyst Q&A not held [Unconfirmed].\nAll 37 points addressed; the two data flags are carried into scenarios\n(via capex/tax assumptions), not buried.\n\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25