uggests smart-money skepticism of the growth narrative.\n- Institutional ownership: 89.39%; passive/ETF flows will amplify any sentiment shift [Actual]\n- Insider ownership: 19.7% \u2014 strong alignment, but no recent insider net-buy signal [Actual]\n- Options: [Unconfirmed \u2014 no put/call data in pack or retrieval]\n- Analyst targets: mean $171.53, median $168, low $128, high $250 [Actual]. Distribution skews bullish. My IV ($128) exactly matches the LOWEST analyst target \u2014 a yellow flag for sell-side complacency.\n- Crowding risk: MODERATE (7/15) \u2014 89% institutional ownership means forced-selling risk if fundamentals disappoint; high passive index weight.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- PCTY offers an uncorrelated HCM/payroll stream to a typical large-cap tech portfolio; its SMB cyclicality is unique vs. mega-cap software.\n- However, its 30%+ drawdown in the last 52 weeks (from $182.83 to $152.77, with a $92.99 low) demonstrates significant drawdown sensitivity [Actual].\n- For a growth-leaning portfolio: PCTY's role is as a DEFENSIVE COMPOUNDER. It fits a \"quality value\" sleeve, not a momentum or high-growth sleeve.\n- If portfolio already holds ADP/PAYX, owning PCTY adds concentrated HCM exposure \u2014 avoid overlap.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500