IS (using same data):\n1. Growth deceleration is REAL and guided: 11% FY2026 \u2192 ~7% FY2027; the \"double-digit compounder\" story is over, and the multiple should re-rate toward the peer average (~22x vs current 28x).\n2. SBC is a permanent cost: $139M/yr (7.8% of revenue). The \"$428M FCF\" is cosmetic \u2014 true economic FCF after SBC and the one-time tax benefit is ~$254M; the stock trades at ~30x that number.\n3. One-time tax benefit inflated FY2026: management itself called FY2027 a \"difficult comparison\" \u2014 the reported FCF margin expansion of 270bps is partly artifact.\n4. The accounting change (7\u21928yr deferred contract cost amortization) manufactures 120-140bps of EBITDA margin expansion. This is fake operational leverage and invites auditing scrutiny.\n5. Float dependence: $120M interest income is rate-driven; guidance already cuts it to $103M. Two more cuts could take it to $80M, making reported revenue growth look ~5-6%.\n6. Competitive moat is narrowing: 0.29% market share vs Microsoft 52%; ADP/Paychex have larger scale and can replicate AI features.\n7. Valuation: at $152.77, you pay $128 of value (my DCF) and get zero downside protection; the lowest sell-side target is $128.\n\nStep 9-2. LOGIC COMBAT (Long vs Short):\n- Long strength: 7/10 (strong execution, wide moat, excellent capital allocation, AI engagement growth)\n- Short strength: 8/10 (growth deceleration, SBC-adjusted economics, accounting maneuvers, float dependence)\n- GAP = 1 < 2 \u2192 MANDATORY CONVICTION DOWNGRADE applied in Section 5 (High \u2192 Medium).\n- Verdict: The short case is not fully persuasive (it does not justify outright collapse), but it is strong enough to negate a \"Buy.\" This is a HOLD/AVOID.\n\nStep 9-3. ADVERSARIAL DATA:\n- No active short-seller report (Hindenburg, etc.) found in retrieved sources \u2014 noted as absence of evidence, not evidence of safety.\n- No activist campaign identified in retrieved sources [Unconfirmed].\n- Risk factors disclosed in 10-K were cited in web research (AI governance, pay transparency, cybersecurity) but no full text retrieved [Unconfirmed].\n\nStep 9-4. KILLED ARGUMENTS (dismissed and why):\n- \"AI will double growth\": Dismissed \u2014 the company's own FY2027 guidance embeds only 7% growth despite Layering AI modules; no hard evidence of AI-attached pricing in the data pack [Unconfirmed].\n- \"Float income will normalize as recurring revenue\": Partially dismissed \u2014 $103M guided FY2027 (still material), but if rates stay at 3.5%, the fair value of the float franchise is ~$80-90M, not growing.\n- \"Buybacks prove management confidence\": Partially dismissed \u2014 buybacks at $142 average were reasonable, but they also merely offset SBC dilution and the debt-funded portion weakens the balance sheet.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPASS/FAIL across 37 audit points (summary):\nA. Methodology: PASS \u2014 Engine selected after archetype transition check; no DCF-only conclusion (multiples cross-check included).\nB. Valuation: PASS \u2014 WACC, tax rate, capex, D&A, \u0394WC all explicitly sourced; key assumption (\u0394WC = 0) disclosed as a judgment call due to float-driven volatility.\nC. Bias: PASS \u2014 Red team downgrade applied; low analyst target equals my IV; no confirmation bias.\nD. Consistency: PASS \u2014 no mixing of GAAP OI and company non-GAAP FCF; SBC treated consistently as an expense; no double-counting. Note: earlier reconciliation confirmed SBC is inside GAAP operating income; no separate deduction