arter; add at $117 and $108 as macro confirms (credit spreads stable, Fed cuts without recession).\n- THESIS KPI MONITORING: client count growth (\u22655% annual), ARPC growth (\u22654% annual), revenue retention (\u226592%), adjusted EBITDA margin ex-float (\u226532%), SBC/revenue (\u22648%), total capex/revenue (\u22646%).\n- HIGH-CONFIDENCE STATEMENT: PCTY is a high-quality, wide-moat, well-managed HCM compounder with an excellent balance sheet. It is a GOOD BUSINESS at a RICH PRICE. The market is paying for 5% terminal growth at a 9.5% discount rate \u2014 beyond what the guided growth trajectory supports. Price must decline ~20% to offer adequate compensation for the risks identified.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 END OF REPORT \u2014 RS2 v2.0 ENGINE\n\u25a0 DISCLAIMER: This is an analytical model output, not investment advice. All [Assumption]/[Estimate]/[Unconfirmed] tags reflect data quality limits. Never invest solely on the basis of a single valuation model.\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n```"}, {"sample": 3, "iv": 144.0, "plausible": true, "reasons": [], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "secs": 316, "report": "```\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 PCTY \u2014 PAYLOCITY HOLDING CORP.\n\u25a0 RS2 v2.0 INTEGRATED INVESTMENT ANALYSIS\n\u25a0 T0: 2026-08-24 | Price: $152.765 | Mkt Cap: $8.458B\n\u25a0 Analyst: RS2 Engine | Formal English Output\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nSECTION 0. ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u25a0 LAYER 0 \u2014 ENTERPRISE CLASSIFICATION & MODEL SELECTION\n\nStep 0-1. Archetype Determination: B \u2014 QUALITY COMPOUNDER\n  Justification (3+ reasons):\n  1. Revenue growth 11% (FY26) with gross margin 69.2% and operating\n     margin 21.8% \u2014 a mature, profitable growth profile, not a binary\n     option or turnaround [Actual].\n  2. Recurring revenue model: 92%+ revenue retention on 44,400\n     clients [Actual, company call]; mission-critical payroll drives\n     switching costs.\n  3. FCF margin 24.2% (company non-GAAP definition) and ROIC >25%\n     [Estimate from filed data] \u2014 consistent with quality compounding.\n  4. Balance sheet structurally clean: net cash ~$139M [Estimate].\n\nStep 0-2. Valuation Engine: ENGINE 1 (Traditional DCF + Multiples).\n  Rationale: Stable recurring cash flows with clear profitability\n  history; no cyclical normalization (Engine 2) required; no dominant\n  platform optionality (Engine 3) \u2014 the AI narrative is incremental,\n  not the core value driver; no binary regulatory path (Engine 5).\n\nStep 0-3. Archetype Transition: NONE.\n  PCTY is transitioning from Fast-Grower towards Stalwart (Lynch\n  classification), but this does not change archetype B classification.\n  Growth has decelerated from ~38% (FY23) to 11% (FY26) and guided to\n  ~7% (FY27) [Actual]; the deceleration is a maturity path, not a\n  business-model transition. No blended engine required.\n\nStep 0-4. Engine Selection Justification:\n  Why this archetype: 12 years of profitable operation, 92% retention,\n  strong FCF conversion, capital-light model.\n  Why Engine 1: DCF anchors value on observable cash flows and margins;\n  multiples provide cross-check.\n  Alternative engine error: Engine 4 (expectation-driven) would\n  over-weight the AI/optionality narrative; Engine 3 would mix core\n  SaaS (quality) with platform premium (product hybrid) without\n  numerical backing.\n\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 1-1. Macro Variables [Actual/Estimate, sources cited]:\n  \u2022 10Y Treasury yield: ~4.70% (Aug 21, 2026, TradingEconomics,\n    YCharts; \"highest since 2025\" per Bloomberg Aug 18, 2026).\n    Direction: rising (+0.44pts YoY). [Actual]\n  \u2022 Real rates: 10Y TIPS implied ~1.8% [Estimate \u2014 derived from\n    nominal yield minus breakeven inflation assumptions].\n  \u2022 Fed funds rate: 3.50\u20133.75% \u2014 on hold for 5 consecutive FOMC\n    meetings as of July 2026 [Actual, FOMC minutes / Forbes];\n    markets price ~1-in-3 chance of a hike [Estimate].\n  \u2022 DXY: 98.93 (Aug 25, 2026, TradingEconomics); dollar weak and\n    falling over the past month. [Actual]\n  \u2022 Fed guidance embedded in PCTY FY27 guide: two 25bp cuts in 2H\n    FY27 (per company call). [Actual]\n  \u2022 Global liquidity: bond-selloff \"rout\" in thin August trading,\n    corporate debt supply heavy (Bloomberg). [Estimate]\n  \u2022 Economic cycle: mature expansion, late-cycle signals; SMB\n    sentiment \"softening\" per industry sources. [Estimate]\n  \u2022 Credit spreads: not specifically sourced [Unconfirmed]; assumed\n    normal-to-tightening.\n\nStep 1-2. Regime Probability Distribution (\u03a3=100%):\n  Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 25%\n  Reflation (high rates + growth): 35%\n  Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 20%\n  Recession (low rates + low growth): 20%\n  [Assumption \u2014 based on Fed on-hold with hike risk, rising 10Y,\n  soft SMB sentiment.]\n\nStep 1-3. Enterprise Macro Sensitivity (each axis \u22123 to +3):\n  Interest rate sensitivity: \u22121.5 (long-duration SaaS multiples\n    compress; float income declines with cuts)\n  Dollar sensitivity: \u22120.5 (minimal FX exposure; US-centric)\n  Liquidity sensitivity: +1.0 (low leverage; net cash)\n  Economic cycle sensitivity: \u22121.5 (payroll volumes and SMB hiring\n    tied to employment cycle)\n  Commodity sensitivity: \u22120.5 (indirect via SMB cost base)\n\nStep 1-4. Macro Alignment:\n  Weighted impact = 0.25\u00d7(+)\u2026 \u2248 \u22120.6 \u2192 HEADWIND (mild).\n  Consequence: Conviction \u22120.5 steps; strengthen split-entry\n  discipline. [No change to intrinsic value.]\n\nSECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 1.5-1. Base Rate Inquiry:\n  \u2022 Quality SaaS (Archetype B) 5-year survival: >85% [Base rate \u2014\n    established, high-retention software].\n  \u2022 Profitable within 5 years: >90% (already in year 12 of GAAP\n    profitability). [Actual]\n  \u2022 AI platform transition success: ~20\u201330% [Base rate for platform\n    pivots]. However, PCTY's AI expansion is incremental module\n    attach (Ignite AI, Aidora, Grayscale) \u2014 not a business-model\n    replacement.\n  \u2022 M&A at this scale (>$100M) achieving ROIC > WACC: ~40%\n    [Base rate]; Aidora/Grayscale deal values not disclosed\n    [Unconfirmed].\n\nStep 1.5-2. Deviation from Base Rate:\n  My base case implies 50% probability of meeting base IV and 75%\n  of not losing money. Deviation above base rate justified by:\n  1. 92%+ revenue retention [Actual] \u2014 proves switching-cost moat.\n  2. 12 consecutive years of positive OCF, 8 years positive net\n     income [Actual].\n  3. 25% of new business flows through broker channel [Actual] \u2014\n     predictable distribution advantage.\n  S U F F I C I E N T justification. No red-flag re-evaluation.\n\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2-1. Business Understanding (3 sentences):\n  Paylocity provides cloud payroll and human-capital-management\n  (HCM) software to mid-market SMBs (44,400 clients). Revenue is\n  recurring SaaS fees plus interest on client funds held for payroll\n  tax remittance (~$119.96M float income in FY26, 6.8% of revenue).\n  The company is expanding into spend management, AI-agent\n  workflows (Ignite AI), and retirement.\n  Understandability: HIGH.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat Assessment (0\u20133 each):\n  Intangible assets (trust/brand in payroll): 2\n  Switching costs (payroll, tax compliance): 3\n  Network effects: 1\n  Cost advantage: 1\n  Economies of scale: 2\n  Regulatory barriers (tax/regulatory complexity): 2\n  Data moat: 1\n  TOTAL: 12/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT.\n  Moat direction: STABLE to WIDENING \u2014 retention stable at 92%+,\n  ARPU rising +5.4%, module attach (Retirement, Spend, AI) increases\n  switching costs.\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch Classification: FAST GROWER \u2192 STALWART (transition).\n  Key checks: growth decelerating (38%\u219211%\u21927% guided); FCF strong;\n  balance sheet clean. Valuation discipline is the controlling\n  variable \u2014 this is a mature compounder, not a hypergrowth stock.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard (FY2026 unless noted):\n  \u2022 Revenue growth: 11.0% (1-yr), 22.8% (5-yr CAGR) [Actual]\n  \u2022 Operating margin: 21.8% (vs 10.8% 12-yr median) [Actual]\n  \u2022 Net income growth: +18.8% to $270M [Actual]\n  \u2022 ROE: ~22.0% [Estimate, vendor]\n  \u2022 ROIC (GAAP): ~28% [Estimate \u2014 NOPAT/IC, see 2.5]\n  \u2022 FCF margin: 24.2% [Actual, company non-GAAP]\n  \u2022 Net debt: NET CASH ~$139M [Estimate \u2014 cash $272M less debt\n    components; see 2.5]\n  \u2022 Interest coverage: >30\u00d7 [Estimate \u2014 interest expense low after\n    $81.3M debt repayment FY26]\n  VERDICT: EXCELLENT.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (Total 15):\n  1. Buyback efficiency: 2/3 \u2014 $398.1M repurchased FY26, 2.8M\n     shares at avg ~$142, within 52-wk range $93\u2013183 (mid-range).\n     Positive: share count \u22123.1% [Actual].\n  2. M&A track record: 2/3 \u2014 Aidora/Grayscale subscale, \"not\n     material\" impact [Actual]; impairment history not disclosed\n     [Unconfirmed].\n  3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 \u2014 capital-light; incremental ROIC >20%\n     [Estimate].\n  4. Rationality of mix: 3/3 \u2014 R&D 14.5% of revenue + buybacks +\n     small tuck-ins. Balanced.\n  5. Guidance accuracy: 3/3 \u2014 FY26 guidance raised twice then\n     beaten; Q4 EPS $1.84 vs Zacks consensus $1.54 [Actual].\n  Insider bonus: CEO/insider ownership 19.7% (+1 pt); no large\n  recent insider net-sell flagged.\n  TOTAL: 14/15.\n\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization:\n  Non-GAAP R&D = 14.5% of revenue \u2248 $257M [Actual, company call].\n  Capitalize 50% over 4-yr life [Assumption]. Net add-back to\n  operating income \u2248 $50M. Adjusted operating income \u2248 $436M.\n  Adjusted invested capital \u2248 $1,382M (equity $1.221B + debt\n  $133M \u2212 cash $272M + R&D pool ~$300M [Estimate]).\n  Adjusted ROIC \u2248 29% (vs GAAP ~28%). No material gap \u2014 SBC already\n  expensed in GAAP; R&D capitalization does not change the story.\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC Treatment:\n  SBC FY26 = $139M [Actual]. Owner FCF = OCF $533M \u2212 broad capex\n  ~$105M \u2212 SBC $139M \u2248 $289M [Estimate]. SBC is ~36% of GAAP\n  operating income; treated as a real expense in the DCF (GAAP EBIT).\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization:\n  Operating leases $52M [Actual, FY26]. Adjusted net debt =\n  LT debt $81M + leases $52M \u2212 cash $272M \u2212 ST investments $0M\n  [Actual] \u2248 NET CASH $139M.\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data Assets: not separately valued; HCM data\n  embedded in retention economics and ARPU growth. [Assumption]\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC: ~29% vs GAAP ~28% \u2014 gap <5pts, no\n  adjustment-driven conclusion change.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett):\n  NI $270M + D&A $112M \u2212 maintenance capex ~$60M [Estimate \u2014\n  broad capex $105M less growth portion] \u2212 \u0394WC (neutral) \u2248 $322M\n  [Estimate]. Equates to ~3.8% of market cap.\n\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 3-1. Discount Rate Derivation:\n  Risk-free rate: 4.70% [Actual \u2014 10Y UST, Aug 21 2026]\n  ERP: 4.5% [Assumption \u2014 long-run US equity risk premium]\n  Beta: 0.90 [Assumption \u2014 blended: vendor 0.433 [Aggregator] and\n    Investing.com 5-year beta 0.95 [Estimate]; 0.90 reflects\n    recurring-revenue defensiveness while avoiding under-stating\n    duration risk]\n  Cost of equity = 4.70 + 0.90 \u00d7 4.5 = 8.75%\n  Cost of debt = 5.8% pre-tax [Assumption SOFR+150bps] \u00d7 (1\u221222%) =\n    4.52%\n  Capital weights: E = $8.458B, D = $0.133B = 1.5% D\n  WACC = 8.75 \u00d7 0.985 + 4.52 \u00d7 0.015 = 8.69% \u2248 8.7%\n\nStep 3-2. Explicit Forecast (per-year, $M except noted):\n  SOURCING DISCIPLINE: FY27 revenue = company guidance midpoint\n  $1.8875B (+6.6%) [Actual]. FY28+ growth, margins, capex = my\n  [Assumption], informed by: FY26 Adjusted EBITDA margin 37.0%, FY27\n  guidance $690\u2013700M (36.5\u201337.1%), FY27 guidance assumes flat\n  workforce levels, float income declining to $103M, and industry\n  maturation. HCM market growth beyond FY27 not independently\n  retrievable within research budget [Unconfirmed]; sensitivity\n  shown.\n\n  | $M | FY26A | FY27E | FY28E | FY29E | FY30E | FY31E | FY32E |\n  | Revenue | 1,771 | 1,888 | 2,011 | 2,122 | 2,228 | 2,328 | 2,421 |\n  | Growth% | 11.0 | 6.6 | 6.5 | 5.5 | 5.0 | 4.5 | 4.0 |\n  | Op margin% | 21.8 | 22.5 | 23.3 | 24.0 | 24.6 | 25.1 | 25.5 |\n  | EBIT | 386 | 425 | 469 | 509 | 548 | 584 | 617 |\n  | NOPAT (t=22%) | 301 | 331 | 366 | 397 | 428 | 456 | 482 |\n  | D&A (6%\u21925.9% rev) | 112 | 113 | 121 | 127 | 134 | 140 | 145 |\n  | Broad capex (5.5%) | 105 | 104 | 111 | 117 | 123 | 128 | 133 |\n  | \u0394WC [Assumption, neutral] | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n  | UFCF | 308 | 341 | 376 | 408 | 439 | 468 | 494 |\n  Sources: FY26 actuals [Filed]; FY27 revenue and EBITDA guidance\n  [Actual, transcript]; FY27 op margin = guided EBITDA de-risked for\n  float income decline and accounting-change benefit [Estimate];\n  FY28+ [Assumption].\n  Note: \u0394WC neutral based on 5-yr average \u2248 +$29M (near zero)\n  [Arithmetic on filed WC].\n\nStep 3-3. Terminal Value:\n  Terminal growth = 3.5% [Assumption \u2014 long-run nominal US GDP].\n  WACC = 8.7%. TV = FY32 FCF \u00d7 1.035 / (0.087 \u2212 0.035) =\n  494 \u00d7 1.035 / 0.052 = $9,827M [Arithmetic].\n\nStep 3-4. Intrinsic Value:\n  PV explicit UFCF (6 years @ 8.7%): $1,870M [Arithmetic]\n  PV terminal: $5,957M [Arithmetic]\n  EV: $7,827M [Arithmetic]\n  + Net cash (cash $272M \u2212 vendor debt $133M): +$139M\n    [Estimate; vendor total debt 0.133B; lease-adjusted net cash\n    identical]\n  Equity value: $7,966M\n  Shares: 55.366M [Actual]\n  \u2192 INTRINSIC VALUE (BASE): $143.9 per share.\n  50% CI: $130\u2013$160 | 80% CI: $108\u2013$190 [Estimate \u2014 parameter\n  ranges below]\n\nStep 3-5. Sensitivity (Tornado \u2014 Top 3 variables):\n  1. WACC: 8.2% \u2192 $154 | 9.2% \u2192 $135 [Estimate]\n  2. Terminal growth: 3.0% \u2192 $136 | 4.0% \u2192 $155 [Estimate]\n  3. FY30 operating margin: 24.0% vs 19.6% (2024 level) \u2192\n     $141 / $158 range [Estimate]\n  These three variables become Thesis KPIs (see Section 8).\n\nStep 3-6. Multiples Cross-Check (at IV $144):\n  Forward P/E (FY27E EPS $6.07 [Estimate]) = 23.7\u00d7\n  Peer context: ADP ~24\u00d7 fwd, PAYX ~19\u00d7 fwd [Estimate \u2014 from\n  market data; not independently re-sourced]. PCTY deserves upper\n  range: faster growth + 37% EBITDA margin.\n  EV/Sales FY27 = 4.15\u00d7 [Arithmetic] \u2014 reasonable for a 7%\n  grower; not a premium.\n  EV/Adjusted EBITDA FY27 (midpoint $695M) = 11.3\u00d7 [Arithmetic \u2014\n  but adjusted EBITDA excludes SBC and includes float income; GAAP\n  EV/EBITDA = 14.5\u00d7, the more conservative gauge].\n  Reverse DCF: current price $152.77 implies WACC ~8.2% or revenue\n  growth ~1.5\u20132pts higher in FY28\u201330 [Estimate]. Feasible but\n  requires AI attach to re-accelerate growth \u2014 NOT my base case.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive Response:\n  ADP/Paychex already compete; if PCTY's Ignite AI wins share,\n  incumbents can replicate features quickly. Price-war risk: \u22121\n  [Assumption]. Microsoft-scale entry would be the real disruptor\n  (SharePoint/Teams HCM embed), but payroll tax compliance is a\n  credible barrier. Net: \u22121.\n\nStep 3.5-2. Reflexivity:\n  Positive: SBC ($139M) is a talent/retention tool; high stock\n  supports acquisition currency (Aidora/Grayscale were stock+cash\n  likely). Negative: a prolonged de-rating would inflate SBC\n  dilution cost and impede M&A. Today, neutral-positive [Estimate].\n\nStep 3.5-3. Customer Behavior Evolution:\n  Early-adopter AI customers \u2192 mainstream. Management: \"AI\n  interactions nearly doubled quarter over quarter\" [Actual].\n  As penetration grows, ARPU expansion (+5.4% in FY26) may face\n  churn headwinds from price-sensitive SMBs. LTV/CAC payback is\n  short per web sources [Estimate \u2014 not independently verifiable].\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 4-1/2. Scenario Composition (\u03a3=100%; Base = highest p):\n  BEAR (25%): SMB employment recession; revenue growth falls to\n    3\u20134% by FY29; OM stalls at 20%; float income compressed;\n    WACC 9.5%; terminal 2.5%. IV \u2248 $100.\n  BASE (50%): my DCF path \u2192 IV \u2248 $144.\n  BULL (25%): Ignite AI attach drives ARPU >7% and client growth\n    re-accelerates; revenue +8% FY28\u201330, OM reaches 29%; WACC 8.3%;\n    terminal 4%. IV \u2248 $210.\n  (All scenarios [Estimate/Assumption]; probabilities are my\n  posterior judgment.)\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian Update:\n  Prior (base rate): 70% probability of quality SaaS compounder\n  hitting base-case within \u00b120% [Estimate]. Updated by: (a)\n  FY27 guidance at 7% \u2014 consistent with my fade, (b) management\n  execution record (3/3 beats), (c) float income decline \u2014 a known\n  \u200edrag, (d) two Federal Reserve cuts embedded in guidance.\n  Posterior: Base 50%, Bear 25%, Bull 25% [Assumption].\n\nStep 4-4/5. Expected Value & Margin of Safety:\n  Expected Price = 0.25\u00d7100 + 0.50\u00d7144 + 0.25\u00d7210 = $149.50.\n  Expected return vs T0 $152.77 = \u22122.1% [Arithmetic].\n  MoS (Base) = (144 \u2212 152.77) / 144 = \u22126.1% \u2192 NONE.\n  MoS (Expected) = (149.5 \u2212 152.77) / 149.5 = \u22122.2% \u2192 NONE.\n  50% CI: $100\u2013$210; 80% CI (with tails): $88\u2013$235 [Estimate].\n\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 4.5-1/2:\n  Market implied horizon: forward P/E 25.2\u00d7 \u2192 the market is\n  effectively pricing ~5\u20136 years of 7% growth then a 3.5% fade,\n  roughly my base path [Estimate].\n  My horizon: 3\u20135 years.\n  Spread: 0\u20131 years \u2192 NO ARBITRAGE.\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 5-1. Conviction Score (Total 15):\n  Business Quality: 3/3 (wide moat, 92% retention)\n  Valuation Attractiveness: 1/3 (MoS negative)\n  Macro Alignment: 2/3 (neutral-mild headwind)\n  Thesis Clarity: 3/3 (KPIs: client growth, ARPU, retention, OM)\n  Execution Traceability: 3/3 (12-yr record, raised guidance twice\n    in FY26)\n  TOTAL: 12/15 \u2192 HIGH conviction.\n  Macro headwind: \u22120.5 steps \u2192 still HIGH.\n  Conviction decay: \u22121 per 6 months absent confirmation.\n\nStep 5-2. Sizing: High conviction allows 6\u20138% max weight in normal\n  conditions, but MoS < 0% OVERRIDES \u2014 no new position at T0.\n  Positioning guidance: 0% new money; entry only at $125\u2013135 zone\n  (MoS 6\u201315%).\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  Short interest: 7.0% of float, 2.98M shares, 4.28 days-to-cover,\n  +8.2% MoM [Actual, Aggregator]. Moderate bearish crowd; squeeze\n  potential exists but not extreme.\n  Institutional ownership: 89.39% [Actual, Aggregator] \u2014 very high;\n  vulnerability to passive ETF outflows (no dividend, so only price\n  momentum drives flows).\n  Insider: 19.7% ownership [Actual] \u2014 strong alignment.\n  Options positioning: not retrievable [Unconfirmed].\n  Sentiment: sell-side mean $171.53, median $168.0, low $128, high\n  $250 [Actual] \u2014 modestly bullish, not extreme.\n  Crowding Risk Score: 6/15 (high institutional ownership, moderate\n  short crowding). Position size penalty: \u22121%p applicable only when\n  a position exists.\n\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  Sector: Technology / Software-Application. If the portfolio is\n  already tech-heavy, PCTY adds low-beta diversification (beta 0.43\u2013\n  0.95 [Aggregator/Estimate]). If portfolio is value-oriented, PCTY\n  introduces growth-style duration risk with no dividend.\n  Historical correlation with 2022-style rate shocks: high (all\n  long-duration SaaS de-rated together). Prefer [Assumption] modest\n  allocation \u22645% when valuation permits \u2014 currently it does not.\n\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  Kelly formula = Edge / Odds.\n  Edge = Expected price \u2212 Current price = $149.50 \u2212 $152.77 = \u2212$3.27\n  [Arithmetic].\n  Odds (upside if correct, bear/truncated): ~$60 upside vs ~$50\n  downside in scenarios \u2192 Kelly \u2248 \u22123% \u2192 KELLY = 0%.\n  Fractional Kelly (quarter): 0%.\n  Layer 5 (High conviction sizing 6\u20138%) vs Layer 6.5 (0%) gap =\n  6\u20138% < 20%p threshold \u2014 no re-analysis required; the SIZING\n  OVERRIDE is MoS < 0%, which is the correct resolution.\n\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  Risks:\n  1. Float income decline: FY27 guided $103M vs $119.96M FY26\n     (\u221214%) [Actual] \u2014 revenue-quality headwind.\n  2. SMB employment cycle: guidance assumes flat workforce levels \u2014\n     any deterioration hits per-employee revenue.\n  3. Competition (ADP/Paychex/Microsoft): scale and AI feature\n     parity risk [Estimate].\n  4. Rate-cut delay: 10Y at 4.7%, Fed on hold \u2014 multiple\n    