    QUARTERLY.\n  5. OM trajectory toward 24% by FY29 \u2014 ANNUAL.\n  Trigger for full re-evaluation: any single quarter with revenue\n  growth <4%, retention <90%, client growth <3%, or OM <19%.\n  Buyback monitoring: continue to expect \u2265$150M/yr [Assumption].\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 9-1. Short Thesis:\n  1. Growth decelerating: 38% (FY23) \u2192 11% (FY26) \u2192 7% guided\n     (FY27) \u2014 a maturity curve that should de-rate the multiple.\n  2. Float income is 6.8% of revenue and shrinking; quality of\n     revenue is lower than headline growth.\n  3. SBC ($139M) = 51% of net income \u2014 true owner earnings from OCF\n     are ~$289M, not the headline $497M filed FCF.\n  4. FY27 EBITDA guidance embeds 120\u2013140bps of benefit from an\n     amortization accounting change \u2014 the \"beat\" quality is\n     accounting-driven.\n  5. FCF margin 24.2% in FY26 included a one-time tax-legislation\n     benefit (management cautioned on FY27 volatility).\n  6. 89.4% institutional ownership + 7% short \u2192 heavy index/passive\n     exposure, no dividend floor.\n  7. At 25\u00d7 forward GAAP EPS, the market pays a growth premium for\n     a grower now at market-growth rate.\n  8. Market share ~0.29% vs Microsoft 52% in adjacent cloud \u2014 the\n     ecosystem threat is real [Estimate, web research].\nStep 9-2. Logic Combat:\n  Long strength: 6/10 (retention, ROIC, capital-light, execution\n  history, insider ownership, FCF).\n  Short strength: 7/10 (deceleration, SBC scale, accounting benefit,\n  float income decline, valuation premium).\n  GAP < 2 \u2192 CONVICTION DOWNGRADE from High to MEDIUM for the\n  purpose of buy initiation. This is consistent with the Hold\n  verdict.\nStep 9-3. Adversarial reports: none identified from Hindenburg-\n  style activists; web brief flagged valuation and compliance\n  concerns only [Unconfirmed \u2014 no dedicated short-seller reports\n  found within research budget].\nStep 9-4. Killed Arguments:\n  \u2022 \"AI will re-accelerate growth to 15%\" \u2014 killed: no net-new\n    revenue disclosed for AI product; it is module attach.\n    Becomes valid if AI ARPU drives ARPU growth >8% for 2 quarters.\n  \u2022 \"Float income is stable recurring revenue\" \u2014 killed: guided down\n    $17M YoY and rate-cut sensitive. Becomes valid if Fed cuts are\n    reversed and yields rise.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  A. Methodology: Engine 1 appropriate; DCF + multiples + reverse\n     DCF; no single-method conclusion. PASS.\n  B. Valuation: explicit 6-year forecast; terminal g \u2264 nominal GDP;\n     WACC derived from current 10Y (4.70%) with blended beta. PASS.\n  C. Bias: Overconfidence flagged \u2014 Scenario CI (80%: $108\u2013$190)\n     is wide relative to the \u22126% MoS \u2192 conclusion does not rely on\n     a single point. PASS.\n  D. Consistency: No mixing of engine types; float income treated\n     as inside revenue (as company does); SBC expensed in GAAP\n     margin path. PASS.\n  E. Narrative: AI/TAM narrative NOT monetized explicitly \u2014 no\n     platform premium included without numeric backing. PASS.\n  F. Red Team: performed (Section 9); downgrade applied. PASS.\n  G. Data Integrity: Capex d