uisition currency (Aidora/Grayscale were stock+cash\n  likely). Negative: a prolonged de-rating would inflate SBC\n  dilution cost and impede M&A. Today, neutral-positive [Estimate].\n\nStep 3.5-3. Customer Behavior Evolution:\n  Early-adopter AI customers \u2192 mainstream. Management: \"AI\n  interactions nearly doubled quarter over quarter\" [Actual].\n  As penetration grows, ARPU expansion (+5.4% in FY26) may face\n  churn headwinds from price-sensitive SMBs. LTV/CAC payback is\n  short per web sources [Estimate \u2014 not independently verifiable].\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 4-1/2. Scenario Composition (\u03a3=100%; Base = highest p):\n  BEAR (25%): SMB employment recession; revenue growth falls to\n    3\u20134% by FY29; OM stalls at 20%; float income compressed;\n    WACC 9.5%; terminal 2.5%. IV \u2248 $100.\n  BASE (50%): my DCF path \u2192 IV \u2248 $144.\n  BULL (25%): Ignite AI attach drives ARPU >7% and client growth\n    re-accelerates; revenue +8% FY28\u201330, OM reaches 29%; WACC 8.3%;\n    terminal 4%. IV \u2248 $210.\n  (All scenarios [Estimate/Assumption]; probabilities are my\n  posterior judgment.)\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian Update:\n  Prior (base rate): 70% probability of quality SaaS compounder\n  hitting base-case within \u00b120% [Estimate]. Updated by: (a)\n  FY27 guidance at 7% \u2014 consistent with my fade, (b) management\n  execution record (3/3 beats), (c) float income decline \u2014 a known\n  \u200edrag, (d) two Federal Reserve cuts embedded in guidance.\n  Posterior: Base 50%, Bear 25%, Bull 25% [Assumption].\n\nStep 4-4/5. Expected Value 